    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i just updated the A records for one of our client sites, but the changes aren't showing up for me yet. i've tried clearing my local cache but nothing. why does dns propagation take so long sometimes?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "DNS changes can take time to propagate because different Internet Service Providers cache records from TTL (Time To Live) values, which may be set high by the domain registrar for performance. Your local browser cache and system DNS settings are just the first step; the delay usually occurs as regional DNS servers worldwide gradually replace the old records with the new ones. This process is normal and depends on how long existing servers were instructed to keep the previous data.",
      "source": "target",
